{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Spring Security for authentication and authorization (U1, U2, U3).",
    "File-based security will use a YAML/Properties file with user credentials and roles, loaded at startup.",
    "LDAP authentication will use Spring Security LDAP with embedded LDAP server for testing.",
    "Role-based access control will use @PreAuthorize annotations and HTTP security configuration.",
    "Kerberized HDFS sink will use Hadoop's UserGroupInformation for Kerberos login with keytab.",
    "Mass-ingest spike will evaluate options like Spring Batch, Apache NiFi, or custom JDBC-based ingestion; outcome is a design document.",
    "HBase sink will use HBase Java client with connection pooling and asynchronous writes.",
    "File Roll sink will use a rolling file appender pattern (size/time based) with configurable serialization.",
    "JMX source will use Spring Integration's JMX notification inbound channel adapter.",
    "All new sinks/sources will follow the existing sink/source interface in the codebase.",
    "Integration tests will use Testcontainers for LDAP, HBase, and possibly a mini HDFS cluster (or real clusters).",
    "Build system: Maven (or Gradle) with added dependencies."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The application is a Spring Boot 2.x/3.x application with Spring Integration.",
    "Existing endpoints are REST controllers on port 9393.",
    "There is a common sink/source framework (e.g., Spring Cloud Stream or custom interfaces) to plug in new sinks/sources.",
    "Developer has access to a Kerberized Hadoop cluster and HBase cluster for integration testing.",
    "The spike (U5) does not require implementation, only research and design documentation.",
    "The team uses Maven for dependency management.",
    "Code review is performed by the developer (self-review) and takes about 4 hours total.",
    "Documentation is written in Markdown and placed in the project's docs folder.",
    "Unit tests use JUnit 5 and Mockito; integration tests use Spring Boot Test and Testcontainers.",
    "The development environment includes JDK 17+, IDE, and necessary tools."
  ],
